  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Chef went to the store in order to buy one can of coke. In the store, they offer NNN cans of coke (numbered 111 through NNN). For each valid iii, the current temperature of the iii-th can is CiC_iCi​ and its price is PiP_iPi​.\n\nAfter buying a can of coke, Chef wants to immediately start walking home; when he arrives, he wants to immediately drink the whole can. It takes Chef MMM minutes to get home from the store.\n\nThe ambient temperature outside is KKK. When a can of coke is outside, its temperature approaches the ambient temperature. Specifically, if its temperature is ttt at some point in time:\n\n\nif t&gt;K+1t \\gt K+1t&gt;K+1, then one minute later, its temperature will be t−1t-1t−1\nif t&lt;K−1t \\lt K-1t&lt;K−1, then one minute later, its temperature will be t+1t+1t+1\nif K−1≤t≤K+1K-1 \\le t \\le K+1K−1≤t≤K+1, then one minute later, its temperature will be KKK\nWhen Chef drinks coke from a can, he wants its temperature to be between LLL and RRR (inclusive). Find the cheapest can for which this condition is satisfied or determine that there is no such can.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1,0001 \\le T \\le 1,0001≤T≤1,000",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\le N \\le 1001≤N≤100",
      "1≤M≤1001 \\le M \\le 1001≤M≤100",
      "∣Ci∣≤50|C_i| \\le 50∣Ci​∣≤50 for each valid iii",
      "∣K∣≤50|K| \\le 50∣K∣≤50",
      "−50≤L≤R≤50-50 \\le L \\le R \\le 50−50≤L≤R≤50",
      "1≤Pi≤1061 \\le P_i \\le 10^61≤Pi​≤106 for each valid iii"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains five space-separated integers NNN, MMM, KKK, LLL and RRR.\nNNN lines follow. For each iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N), the iii-th of these lines contains two space-separated integers CiC_iCi​ and PiP_iPi​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer — the price of the can Chef should buy, or −1-1−1 if it is impossible to buy a can such that Chef's condition is satisfied.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3 2 5 4 6\n1 6\n2 8\n8 10\n3 5 10 20 30\n21 20\n22 22\n23 23",
        "output": "8\n-1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: Chef should buy the second can (with price 888), even though the first can is cheaper. If Chef bought the first can, its temperature would be 333 when he got home, and that is outside the range [4,6][4, 6][4,6].\nExample case 2: No matter which can Chef buys, when he gets home, its temperature will be less than 202020, so there is no suitable can available in the store."
      }
    ]
